From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp2: don't mask PM suspend failure in system-off
 handler

thread_system_off_handler()'s own doc comment says it should return
"0 if OK, other value else" so TF-A can panic on a genuine failure,
but the previous commit's code unconditionally reused a single `res`
variable for both pm_change_state()'s result and
stm32_stpmic2_switch_off()'s result - so a successful SWOFF call
silently overwrote and discarded an earlier pm_change_state()
failure. Uses separate res/pm_res variables and returns
pm_res ? pm_res : res so a real PM failure is never swallowed.

Reviewer note: found via a colleague's code review, not by hardware
testing - this is a genuine correctness fix independent of the RTC
root cause, but on its own wouldn't have surfaced the reported bug
(the actual hang happened inside pm_change_state() itself, before
this return path mattered).

Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp2/stm32mp_pm.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp2/stm32mp_pm.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp2/stm32mp_pm.c
index d312b32..088ebb3 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp2/stm32mp_pm.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp2/stm32mp_pm.c
@@ -30,10 +30,11 @@ unsigned long thread_system_off_handler(unsigned long a0 __unused,
 		((PM_MAX_LEVEL << PM_HINT_PLATFORM_STATE_SHIFT) &
 		  PM_HINT_PLATFORM_STATE_MASK);
 	TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
+	TEE_Result pm_res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;

-	res = pm_change_state(PM_OP_SUSPEND, pm_hint);
-	if (res)
-		EMSG("pm_change_state(SUSPEND) failed: %#"PRIx32, res);
+	pm_res = pm_change_state(PM_OP_SUSPEND, pm_hint);
+	if (pm_res)
+		EMSG("pm_change_state(SUSPEND) failed: %#"PRIx32, pm_res);

 	/*
 	 * Physically cut power via STPMIC2 MAIN_CR.SWOFF. I2C7 (the PMIC
@@ -45,7 +46,13 @@ unsigned long thread_system_off_handler(unsigned long a0 __unused,
 	if (res)
 		EMSG("STPMIC2 switch off failed: %#"PRIx32, res);

-	return res;
+	/*
+	 * Don't let a successful SWOFF call mask an earlier
+	 * pm_change_state() failure: this function's own doc comment
+	 * says a non-zero return makes TF-A panic, which is the correct
+	 * behavior for a genuine PM failure.
+	 */
+	return pm_res ? pm_res : res;
 }

 static uint32_t get_pm_hint(unsigned long a0)
--
